# Code Quality

## Standards

- Keep behavior changes intentional; avoid unrelated refactors in feature work.
- Prefer small, focused functions and components with clear names.
- Avoid `any`; if unavoidable, narrow quickly and document why.
- Handle errors explicitly at boundaries (route handlers, external calls, parsing).
- Validate untrusted input (params, query, body, env-driven values).
- Do not swallow errors silently.

## Code comments

**Principle:** Prefer self-documenting code. Comments explain *why*, not *what*.

### Rules

- Avoid obvious comments that restate the code.
- Comment for non-obvious business rules, tradeoffs, workarounds, or external specs.
- Remove stale TODO/FIXME when you touch the related code.

### Examples to avoid

```typescript
// Set the value
setValue(value);

// Hero section
<section>...</section>
```

### Examples that help

```typescript
// Umami loads via deferred script in layout head
// Workaround: Next Image remotePatterns omit this host in dev
```

## Linting

This repo uses ESLint via `next/core-web-vitals` and `@typescript-eslint/recommended` (see `.eslintrc.json`). Comment style is **not** enforced by custom ESLint rules beyond what those presets provide.

## Scope

Applies to all project source, especially `src/`.
